(vector (map (:adr/authoritative_for (vector "kotoba-lang/bytes の新設と設計根拠" "kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn の kotoba-lang/bytes への依存移行の根拠" "net/turn の実I/O層構築（Phase 2以降）に向けた共有基盤ライブラリの位置づけ")), (:adr/supersedes (vector)), (:adr/superseded_by (vector)), (:adr/topic "telecom-independent-substrate-dtn-rcs-mesh-satellite"), (:adr/related (vector "90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607161951-kotoba-lang-dtn-replay-protection.edn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/bytes" "orgs/kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn" "orgs/kotoba-lang/net")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:adr/id "adr-2607161956-kotoba-lang-bytes-shared-primitives-extraction"), (:adr/doc_type :adr), (:adr/last_verified "2026-07-16"), (:adr/body "---\nid: adr-2607161956-kotoba-lang-bytes-shared-primitives-extraction\ntitle: \"ADR-2607161956: kotoba-lang/bytes — shared byte-vector/SHA-1 primitives extracted from kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn (Phase 1 of a net/turn/dtn shared-lib consolidation)\"\nstatus: accepted\ndoc_type: adr\ntopic: telecom-independent-substrate-dtn-rcs-mesh-satellite\nauthoritative: true\nlast_verified: 2026-07-16\nauthoritative_for:\n  - kotoba-lang/bytes の新設と設計根拠\n  - kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn の kotoba-lang/bytes への依存移行の根拠\n  - net/turn の実I/O層構築（Phase 2以降）に向けた共有基盤ライブラリの位置づけ\nrelated:\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn\n  - 90-docs/adr/2607161951-kotoba-lang-dtn-replay-protection.edn\n  - orgs/kotoba-lang/bytes\n  - orgs/kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn\n  - orgs/kotoba-lang/dtn\n  - orgs/kotoba-lang/net\nsupersedes: []\nsuperseded_by: []\n---\n\n# ADR-2607161956: kotoba-lang/bytes — shared byte-vector/SHA-1 primitives extracted from kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn (Phase 1 of a net/turn/dtn shared-lib consolidation)\n\n**Status**: accepted\n**Date**: 2026-07-16\n**Deciders**: Jun Kawasaki\n\n## Problem\n\nAfter the `kotoba-lang/dtn` gap-closing series (ADR-2607161743 through\nADR-2607161951), the user directed: *「net, turn をちゃんと実装, 共有libを設計して\n効率化, 依存効率化」* — properly implement `kotoba-lang/net` and\n`kotoba-lang/turn`'s real I/O (both were, like `dtn` before\nADR-2607161817, protocol-semantics-only with zero network I/O), and do so\nby designing a shared library rather than duplicating plumbing across\nthree repos.\n\nA quick read-only audit of both repos before writing any code surfaced two\nfacts that reshaped the plan:\n\n1. Neither `kotoba-lang/net` (`kotoba.net.gossip`/`kotoba.net.bitswap` —\n   pure fanout/dedup/want-have semantics) nor `kotoba-lang/turn` (STUN\n   codec + credential mint/verify) has ANY real socket I/O — both\n   explicitly name \"actual network I/O\", \"NAT traversal\", and \"peer\n   discovery\" as out of scope in their own READMEs, the same honest-scoping\n   discipline `dtn` itself used before ADR-2607161817. Building real I/O\n   for either is a genuinely new build, not a \"wire dtn to an existing\n   capability\" integration — the earlier gap inventory had understated\n   this.\n2. `kotoba-lang/turn` already has exactly the class of shared primitive\n   `dtn`'s TCP transport (ADR-2607161817) currently reimplements ad-hoc:\n   `kotoba.turn.bytes` (portable byte-vector codecs — u16/u32 BE, XOR,\n   padding, base64) and `kotoba.turn.sha1` (pure SHA-1/HMAC-SHA1, no\n   platform crypto API, byte-identical on JVM and ClojureScript). Neither\n   is actually TURN/STUN-specific; they were simply built there first.\n\nThis ADR is Phase 1 of the resulting plan: extract the generic primitives\nbefore building new I/O on top of anything, so `dtn`'s future transport\nrefactor (Phase 2), `turn`'s real relay I/O (Phase 3), and `net`'s real\ngossip I/O (Phase 4) all draw from one shared foundation instead of each\nreinventing byte-level plumbing.\n\n## Decision\n\n### Decision 1: extract, don't duplicate — `kotoba.turn.bytes`/`kotoba.turn.sha1` move to a new `kotoba-lang/bytes` repo\n\n`src/kotoba/bytes.cljc` (was `kotoba.turn.bytes`) and\n`src/kotoba/bytes/sha1.cljc` (was `kotoba.turn.sha1`) are exact\nmove-and-rename extractions — same functions, same docstrings, same\nimplementations, verified byte-for-byte identical except for the `ns` and\n`require` lines. `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn` no longer owns this code; it\ndepends on `kotoba-lang/bytes` via `:local/root \"../bytes\"`, the same\nsibling-checkout dependency pattern every other `kotoba-lang` library in\nthis workspace already uses.\n\n### Decision 2: this is a mechanical refactor, verified by identical behavior, not a rewrite\n\nThe correctness bar for this ADR is narrow and strict: `turn`'s actual\nSTUN/credential behavior must be provably unchanged. Before the refactor,\n`turn` had 24 deftest / 53 assertions total (bytes + sha1 + credential +\nstun combined) and 0 lint issues. After: `turn` itself has 22 deftest / 43\nassertions (credential's 13/23 and stun's 9/20, untouched) and the new\n`bytes` repo has the 2/10 that moved with `sha1_test`. 43 + 10 = 53 — the\nfull assertion count is conserved across the split, not merely\n\"approximately the same.\" Both repos independently lint clean.\n\n### Decision 3: `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn` is this repo's actual current name — a rename this ADR discovered mid-flight, not caused\n\nWhile registering this work in the manifest, `gh api repos/kotoba-lang/turn`\nresolved to `full_name: \"kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn\"` — the repo was renamed\nat some point before this ADR series began; `kotoba-lang/turn` is now only\na GitHub redirect alias (clones/pushes against the old name still work via\nredirect, which is how the implementing agent's session used it without\nnoticing). `manifest/west.yml` already had it correctly registered as\n`org-ietf-turn` at `orgs/kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn` before this ADR — this\nADR's own pin advance for it uses the correct current name. Recorded here\nso future ADRs in this series reference `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn`, not\nthe stale `kotoba-lang/turn` alias used informally in the Problem section\nabove (quoted there only because that's the name used when the user's\ndirective was issued and the initial research was performed).\n\n### Decision 4: `xor-bytes`/`pad-right`/`base64-decode`/`constant-time-eq` have no direct unit tests — a pre-existing gap, surfaced not created\n\nThe implementing agent found, while trying to move a \"bytes test file\"\nthat turned out not to exist as a standalone unit: `kotoba.turn.bytes` was\nonly ever exercised indirectly (e.g. via `utf8-encode` inside other\nmodules' tests), never directly. This gap predates this extraction — it is\nrecorded here rather than silently carried forward unremarked, matching\nthis workspace's practice of naming coverage gaps explicitly (see\nADR-2607161852/2607161922's own \"known limitation\" sections). Direct unit\ntests for these functions are additive future work, not required to land\nthis extraction (the functions' actual behavior is still exercised,\nindirectly, by every consumer's existing test).\n\n## Verification\n\n- `kotoba-lang/bytes`: `clojure -M:test` → 2 tests / 10 assertions, 0 failures/errors (exactly `turn`'s original `sha1_test.clj`, moved). `clojure -M:lint` → 0 errors, 0 warnings. Pushed to `github.com/kotoba-lang/bytes` (public), commit `263bb0ded79aefb4ab181e659d8b23419b0b9334`. Independently re-verified by the orchestrating session from a cold clone — identical results.\n- `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn`: baseline (before) 24 tests / 53 assertions, 0 lint issues. After: `clojure -M:test` → 22 tests / 43 assertions, 0 failures/errors (credential 13/23 + stun 9/20, both unchanged from baseline). `clojure -M:lint` → 0 errors, 0 warnings. `deps.edn` confirmed depending on `io.github.kotoba-lang/bytes {:local/root \"../bytes\"}`; no stray `bytes.cljc`/`sha1.cljc` files left in `src/`. Pushed, commit `ce6cee2876f4489770e1663d05abd4986fe827f6`. Independently re-verified from a cold clone via the correct canonical URL (`github.com/kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn`) — identical results.\n- `manifest/repos.edn`/`manifest/west.yml`: `bytes` registered via `--entry bytes,org-ietf-turn` (new entry, `:extra-projects` addition), `org-ietf-turn`'s pin advanced (`53643eb61058→ce6cee2876f4`), `verify-west-pins: 2 件の pin 変更をすべて検証 OK` — 5 unrelated pending pin changes elsewhere in the tree correctly left untouched by the scoped `--entry` invocation. Landed via an isolated sibling-path worktree + GitHub API server-side merge, matching every prior ADR in this series.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang` now has one canonical home for portable byte-vector codecs\n  and pure SHA-1/HMAC-SHA1 — `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn`'s own STUN/credential\n  work depends on it rather than owning it, and `dtn`'s Phase 2 transport\n  refactor (next) and `net`'s Phase 4 real-I/O work (later) can depend on\n  the same repo instead of each re-implementing u16/u32 codecs or a pure\n  SHA-1.\n- The \"net/turn ready-made building blocks\" assumption implicit in\n  ADR-2607161743/ADR-2607161922's gap inventories (which named\n  `kotoba-lang/net`/`kotoba-lang/turn` as composition points for peer\n  discovery/NAT traversal as if the capability already existed) is\n  corrected here: both need real, substantial new I/O work of their own\n  before that composition is meaningful — this ADR does not perform that\n  composition, only lays a shared foundation two future phases will build\n  on.\n- `xor-bytes`/`pad-right`/`base64-decode`/`constant-time-eq` remain without\n  direct unit tests (Decision 4) — a known, pre-existing, now-explicitly-\n  recorded gap, not a regression introduced by this extraction.\n- The `kotoba-lang/turn` → `kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn` rename (Decision 3)\n  is now recorded in this ADR series; future work here should use the\n  current name.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- **Leaving `kotoba.turn.bytes`/`kotoba.turn.sha1` inside `turn` and having\n  `dtn`'s (and future `net`'s) transport work depend directly on `turn`**\n  Rejected: `turn` is a STUN/TURN-specific protocol library; making\n  unrelated repos depend on it just to reach two generic utility\n  namespaces would be a confusing, backwards dependency direction — the\n  generic primitives should be the shared root, not a side effect of\n  depending on one specific protocol implementation.\n- **Copy-pasting `kotoba.turn.bytes`/`kotoba.turn.sha1` into `dtn` instead\n  of extracting a shared repo.** Rejected: this is precisely the\n  duplication the user's \"依存効率化\" directive asked to avoid — two\n  divergence-prone copies of the same byte-codec logic instead of one.\n- **Rewriting/\"improving\" the algorithms while moving them.** Rejected:\n  this ADR's whole verification story depends on the move being provably\n  behavior-preserving (Decision 2's conserved assertion count); improving\n  the code, if warranted, is a separate, independently-reviewable future\n  change to `kotoba-lang/bytes` once it exists on its own.\n\n## References\n\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161743-kotoba-lang-rcs-dtn-independent-telecom-substrate.edn`\n- `90-docs/adr/2607161951-kotoba-lang-dtn-replay-protection.edn`\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/bytes/README.edn` — https://github.com/kotoba-lang/bytes\n- `orgs/kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn/README.edn` — https://github.com/kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn\n"), (:adr/artifacts "{:kotoba-lang-bytes \"kotoba-lang/bytes @ 263bb0ded79a (pushed, public)\", :kotoba-lang-org-ietf-turn \"kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn @ ce6cee2876f4 (pushed, public)\", :manifest \"orgs/kotoba-lang/{bytes,org-ietf-turn} registered via --entry bytes,org-ietf-turn, pin-verified\"}"), (:db/id -1), (:adr/authoritative true), (:adr/title "ADR-2607161956: kotoba-lang/bytes — shared byte-vector/SHA-1 primitives extracted from kotoba-lang/org-ietf-turn (Phase 1 of a net/turn/dtn shared-lib consolidation)"), (:adr/source-format "edn")))